WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.860
"Ant-Man &amp; the Wasp: Quantumania"&nbsp;
is almost in theaters, and critics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:09.060
are finally getting a chance to see the&nbsp;
finished product…and they have thoughts…

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.220
When Scott Lang joined the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe in 2015, no one knew what to expect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:20.220
After all, "Ant-Man" was subject to many creative&nbsp;
changes behind the scenes, with the most notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.080
being the departure of original director Edgar&nbsp;
Wright. However, "Ant-Man" and its sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.160
"Ant-Man and the Wasp," have proven to&nbsp;
be exciting additions to the MCU canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.600
giving fans moments of humorous respite&nbsp;
amid the more high-stakes adventures of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.700
the overarching franchise. But does "Ant-Man and&nbsp;
the Wasp: Quantumania" live up to expectations?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.560
The third film in the "Ant-Man" franchise&nbsp;
marks the beginning of Phase 5 of the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.960
so the titular crusader has a lot of weight&nbsp;
to carry on his tiny shoulders. The film sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.500
our heroes forced to try and navigate&nbsp;
the Quantum Realm, which brings them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.660
into contact with strange creatures and their&nbsp;
biggest threat to date — Kang the Conqueror.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.200
"The thing you call a life, will end."

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.900
With that in mind, what do the critics have&nbsp;
to say about Marvel's latest adventure? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.920
general consensus among reviewers on Rotten&nbsp;
Tomatoes is that "Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:17.160
Quantamania" is enjoyable for the most part.&nbsp;
However, as a movie, it's very flawed. Several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:22.020
reviewers pointed out that the film is too focused&nbsp;
on laying the building blocks for Phase 5, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:27.120
comes at the expense of telling a fully-formed&nbsp;
threequel story. Collider's Ross Bonaime wrote,

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:32.566
"Quantumania is a promising, but shaky start&nbsp;
for Phase 5 of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:35.446
it's just a shame it comes at&nbsp;
the sake of the little guy."

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:40.740
Meanwhile, Slashfilm's Jeff Ewing noted that&nbsp;
the film gets Phase 5 off to a promising start,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.340
but it's undercooked in the&nbsp;
grand scheme of things. He says,

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:49.200
"Altogether the film is an engaging and fun&nbsp;
start for the real meat of the Multiverse Saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.354 --> 00:01:52.474
it's also one that needs more&nbsp;
care and detail to flourish."

00:01:52.474 --> 00:01:55.920
For some critics, like Jamie&nbsp;
Broadnax of Black Girl Nerds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.460
the threequel tries to integrate&nbsp;
several genres into its narrative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.720
only to experience an identity&nbsp;
crisis as a result. In her opinion,

00:02:03.886 --> 00:02:07.726
"Tonally this film is different&nbsp;
from the other films. A bit uneven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:11.940
it feels like Jeff Loveness' script wasn't&nbsp;
sure what genre this movie wanted to be."

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.180
That said, IGN Movies' Joshua Yehl believes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.720
Marvel's latest blockbuster has&nbsp;
more pros than cons, writing,

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.620
"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania&nbsp;
has just enough heart, humor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.501
and excellent performances to make up&nbsp;
for its more underdeveloped aspects."

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:31.680
Kang the Conqueror will be the Big Bad of the&nbsp;
MCU for the foreseeable future, with his story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:37.680
set to ramp up and conclude in "Avengers: The Kang&nbsp;
Dynasty" and "Avengers: Secret Wars." Needless to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.840
say, a lot is riding on the franchise's newest&nbsp;
formidable foe, and he has big shoes to fill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.300
considering that Thanos once wiped out half of&nbsp;
the universe with a snap of his fingers. The good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:53.012
news, though, is that based on what critics are&nbsp;
saying the new baddie is off to a flying start.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.327
"I am Kang!"

00:02:55.577 --> 00:03:00.540
Writing for The Guardian, Ellen E Jones praised&nbsp;
Majors' performance and compared the villain to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.380
one of the most morally flawed characters&nbsp;
in the "Star Wars" franchise. She said,

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:10.740
"Majors brings the same emotionally intense it-boy&nbsp;
energy of Adam Driver in The Force Awakens. Note&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.360
how his eyes are often watery with empathy&nbsp;
for his victims, even as he throttles them."

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.620
Elsewhere, The Hollywood Reporter's Frank&nbsp;
Scheck praised Kang as a highlight of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.120
noting that he brings a real sense of&nbsp;
"gravitas" to the proceedings. He writes,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.380
"While it's not surprising that the actor's&nbsp;
imposing physicality perfectly suits his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:33.060
iconic villainous character, he also invests&nbsp;
his performance with such an arrestingly quiet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.900
stillness and ambivalence that you're&nbsp;
on edge every moment he's onscreen."

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.320
USA Today's Brian Truitt echoed these sentiments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.160
stating that Kang's presence covers&nbsp;
up some of the film's flaws, saying,

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:47.460
"Majors thankfully rights&nbsp;
the ship every time he pops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.100
up with his deliciously disconcerting presence."

